# NPM Ignore

# ignore everything
*

# ... but these files
!package.json
!tsconfig.json
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!dist/**
!bundle/**
!types/**

# The CLI entry point and the browser/worker runtime assets it serves. npm force-includes the
# `bin` *target* (bin/tripwire.js) regardless of this file, but not its sibling assets --
# bin/assets/runner-client.js and bin/assets/runner-worker.js are served over HTTP by the dev
# server for the `--target browser`/`--target worker` runs, so without these the published CLI
# ships unable to run either target.
!bin/**

# The opt-in "@nevware21/tripwire/globals" entry (ambient global declarations + the runtime
# installer). Resolved as <package>/globals, so both files must sit at the package root.
!/globals.d.ts
!/globals.js